        "title": "feat(ios): add branded iOS design guide with interactive styling reference",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nThe iOS app currently has no formal design system or style guide. Contributors building new screens or components have no reference for colors, typography, spacing, or component patterns, leading to inconsistent UI across the app.\n\nRelates to #98317\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nA comprehensive branded styling guide was created in Figma and exported as an interactive React app. This PR adds it to the repo at `apps/ios/design-guide/` so contributors can run it locally and reference the exact design tokens, component patterns, and screen mockups when implementing iOS UI.\n\n## What's Included\n\nThe guide covers 6 sections:\n\n| Section | Contents |\n|---|---|\n| **01 Colors** | Brand palette (Claw Red `#E8302A`, Claw Teal `#00C4B0`), surfaces, semantic status colors, text hierarchy, usage rules |\n| **02 Typography** | Three-family stack: Plus Jakarta Sans (headings), DM Sans (body), JetBrains Mono (code/data) with exact size/weight specs |\n| **03 Icons** | Mascot size scale (20pt-96pt), app icon variants, 8 status badge overlays, SF Symbols mapping for all system UI |\n| **04 Components** | 5 button tiers, status badges with glowing dots, iOS-native list rows, text fields (default/focused/error), semantic banners |\n| **05 Screens** | Annotated iPhone mockups: Pending Approval, Agent Chat, Fleet Status |\n| **06 Tokens** | 8pt spacing grid, border radius scale (xs-full), motion/animation tokens (spring, easing) |\n\n### Key Design Decisions\n\n- **Dark-first OLED**: Deep charcoal/void backgrounds optimized for OLED displays\n- **Mascot-derived palette**: Red from body, teal from eyes\n- **Red = primary action only**: One red CTA per screen; teal for accent labels/data only\n- **iOS HIG compliant**: 44pt minimum touch targets, SF Symbols for system UI\n- **Status colors always labeled**: Never color-only\n\n## User Impact\n\nNo runtime impact. This is a design reference that lives at `apps/ios/design-guide/` and is not included in the pnpm workspace or any build pipeline.\n\n## Evidence\n\nScreenshots of all 6 sections are included in `apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/` and rendered in the README.\n\n### Colors\n![Colors](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-01-colors.png)\n\n### Typography\n![Typography](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-02-typography.png)\n\n### Icons\n![Icons](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-03-icons.png)\n\n### Components\n![Components](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-04-components.png)\n\n### Screens\n![Screens](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-05-screens.png)\n\n### Tokens\n![Tokens](https://raw.githubusercontent.com/joelnishanth/openclaw/feat/ios-design-guide/apps/ios/design-guide/screenshots/design-guide-06-tokens.png)\n\n### Running locally\n\n```bash\ncd apps/ios/design-guide\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\n```\n\nFigma source: https://www.figma.com/design/DJ0ad6j0GOuaP1Ozn3B7Dq/Branded-Styling-Guide\n\n---\n\n[Joel Nishanth](https://offlyn.ai) | [offlyn.AI](https://offlyn.ai)\n",
